{
  "slug": "gruyere-and-egg-bistro-salad",
  "title": "Gruyère and Egg Bistro Salad",
  "blurb": "A simple French-style salad with soft-boiled eggs, nutty Gruyère and peppery leaves.",
  "steps": [
    "Bring a pan of water to the boil, lower in the eggs and cook for 6 minutes for soft yolks.",
    "While the eggs cook, whisk together the mustard, vinegar, olive oil, half the salt and half the pepper in a large bowl.",
    "Drain the eggs and run them under cold water, then peel carefully and cut each in half.",
    "Add the salad leaves to the bowl with the dressing and toss gently to coat.",
    "Divide the dressed leaves between four plates and scatter over the shredded Gruyère.",
    "Place two egg halves on each salad, season with the remaining salt and pepper, and serve straight away."
  ],
